<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mandla</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mandla is a town on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narmada-river">Narmada</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madhya-pradesh">Madhya Pradesh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, and the headquarters of Mandla district. It was the later capital of the Gond kingdom of Garha-Mandla, which survived there as a Mughal and then <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> until the Marathas annexed it in 1781. Its riverside fort and temples recall the Gond rulers.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mandla.jpg" alt="Mandla" width="320" height="179" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chintugurb · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Begam_Mahal_Mandla.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
